From 8d6d2a4087fcc69d73e6ca232fe7a2e32a3c0827 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 22:53:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Do not call back() on an empty AV1 slice parameter vector

PackerAV1::SaveSliceData() read slice_params.back() unconditionally. A client
that submits slice data before, or without, any slice parameters therefore
triggered the libstdc++ assertion

  std::vector<_VASliceParameterBufferAV1>::back(): Assertion '!this->empty()'

which aborts the calling process outright -- observed as a Chromium GPU process
dying with exit_code=134. A driver should reject a submission, not kill its
client. Bail out instead.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 utils/packer/packer_av1.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/utils/packer/packer_av1.cpp b/utils/packer/packer_av1.cpp
index d840790..97d9a66 100644
--- a/utils/packer/packer_av1.cpp
+++ b/utils/packer/packer_av1.cpp
@@ -58,6 +58,11 @@ uint32_t PackerAV1::SaveSliceData(void *dst, void *data, uint32_t size)
     if (!dst || !data || size == 0)
         return 0;
 
+    // A client may submit slice data before, or without, any slice parameters.
+    // back() on an empty vector aborts the whole process, so bail out instead.
+    if (slice_params.empty())
+        return 0;
+
     auto slice_param = slice_params.back();
     if (size < slice_param.slice_data_size)
         return 0;
